<<
/A 2178 0 R
/Alt (The four panel diagram shows choropleth maps with associated questions, demonstrating different spatial distribution patterns. Panel a, labelled Cluster, presents a Region Poverty Rate Thematic Map with a legend showing 0 percent to 6 percent, 7 percent to 16 percent, 18 percent to 29 percent, and 33 percent to 71 percent. The map displays regions with varying shades, forming concentrated high or low value groups. Below the map is a question about identifying clusters in the spatial distribution of poverty rate, with choices 0, 1, 2, and 3 clusters. Panel b, labelled Trend, displays a Region Unemployed Population Thematic Map. Its legend shows 22 to 28, 28 to 32, 32 to 36, and 36 to 42. The map exhibits a directional attribute gradient. A question below asks which change characteristic better matches the indicator, with choices Increasing from south to north, Decreasing from west to east, Increasing from southeast to northwest, and Increasing from southwest to northeast. Panel c, labelled Structure, shows a Region Myopia Rate Thematic Map. The legend indicates 22.2 percent to 26.0 percent, 26.8 percent to 30.0 percent, 30.2 percent to 32.4 percent, and 32.6 percent to 36.9 percent. This map contains ring shaped spatial configurations. A question below asks which region is located on the ring structure, with choices DI, AW, TM, and RA.)
/K 36
/P 41 0 R
/Pg 16 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
