/Alt (The three-panel graph shows model accuracy. Panel a displays a bar graph with 20 pairs of vertical bars, each pair representing Discrete and Continuous accuracy for different models. The Discrete bars are consistently taller than the Continuous bars. The Gain values, printed above each pair, range from plus 0.1 to plus 12.1. Panel b shows a bar graph with 12 vertical bars, each representing Accuracy by Hue. Accuracy ranges from 55.2 percentage to 57.6 percentage. The highest accuracy is 57.6 percentage for Yellow 60 degrees, Blue 180 degrees, and Pink 300 degrees. The lowest accuracy is 55.2 percentage for Blue-Purple 210 degrees. Panel c displays four box plots, each representing Accuracy Distribution by Spatial Pattern: Cluster, Trend, Structure, and Random. All box plots show median accuracy between 50 percentage and 70 percentage, with whiskers extending from approximately 30 percentage to 80 percentage.)
