1318 0 obj
<<
/A 2400 0 R
/Alt (The two panel diagram shows thematic maps and text. Panel a, titled A Region Poverty Rate Thematic Map, displays a map with regions labelled with two letter codes. A legend below the map indicates five shades of brown representing poverty rates from 5.0 percent to 26.4 percent. To the right of the map is a question about directional relation reasoning and choices. Below the map and question are two text boxes, Data plus Map and Data only, detailing reasoning processes. Panel b, titled A Region Unemployment Rate Thematic Map, displays a map with regions labelled with two letter codes. A legend below the map indicates five shades of green representing unemployment rates from 0.6 percent to 3.3 percent. To the right of the map is a question about global spatial trend recognition and choices. Below the map and question are two text boxes, Data plus Map and Data only, detailing reasoning processes.)
/K 6
/P 41 0 R
/Pg 30 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
